# Section 4, Element Types / Reference Surfaces: the NEW dialog for 3.2's ref_surf example (a Conic
# Reference, f 5.4, e 0, vertex at the origin, axis +z, zElt 5.4), with NEW's echo of the element (printed before 'Is this correct?') in place of
# 3.2's typed "prescription data" block.  Dave 2026-10-19: Section 4's NEW tutorials become plain
# generated dialogs.  The answers are 3.2's.  3.2's element was the deck's third (its SHOW read iElt= 3)
# in the focused beam of a lens (Figure 21); the setup (not printed) is that: a collimated 1.0 source at
# z=-1 and a plano-hyperbolic lens (flat front at z=-0.2, n 1.5; back at z=-0.1, K -2.25, R -2.75, a
# perfect focus at z=5.4 -- the reference's center), then a FocalPlane at the focus.  Against 3.2's
# dialog: the type menus list more types; the source asks for base units (none) and the refractors for a
# glass type (default FixedIndex); the echo adds nCoat.  The reference is aligned with the wavefront:
# the OPD on it is at the round-off floor.
